[{:seon.task/name "the-process-store-is-made-before-any-shard"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by the walk session: forked-agent tests went red at random under load (seon.repl-test red on 3 agent-process tests, on another run a different one, green alone); one red was :root-did-not-listen, \"Database does not exist\" at target/runs/test-store. Cause, reproduced by the worktree session store at n = 4 shards on a tree without that store: every process test's root opened the one store target/runs/test-store with seon.db/open!, which creates and seeds a store whose data file is missing. Four shards' first roots started at once; one created it, and a root in another shard saw its data file and opened a database not yet made. The first test of shards 2 and 3 went red (seon.agent-test/a-wide-reach-reuses-unchanged-results, an-agent-holds-mains-tests-and-runs-them), and green on a rerun once the store existed. AGENTS section 5 (one store, many branches): the store is made once, before any shard. bin/test seeds it (seon seed 0, as bin/check seeds its store) after building the binary; seon.test-store/process-store names it for root_test and agent_test and refuses, naming bin/test, when it is not made, never creating it. After: the same two namespaces from a fresh tree, all four shards green."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/the-process-store-is-made-before-any-shard}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-test-root-is-its-own"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root: seon.root-test/main-follows-its-source-tree-across-restarts went red under parallel load (4 of 4 on walk's api branch, once on jolt/an-edge-asks-one-way) and green alone. Its first root's fresh main already held the whole Seon program (:removed-forms 71, file-text answering other files). Cause, found by the worktree session store: root_test's root-answers gave every root on the one test store the runs directory <store>-runs. bin/root start in a runs directory whose root still runs only reports that root's status and port (bin/root's start: running, then status), so seon.test-store/start-root! answered another test's root, one that had imported src. The main itself was cut cleanly from :db, which holds no forms after the agent and root tests. Fixed at both producers: root-answers takes a runs directory per main, and start-root! refuses a runs directory a live root holds (:seon.test-store/runs-in-use), never answering that root."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/a-test-root-is-its-own}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-kept-store-is-keyed-by-its-schema"
  :seon.task/plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root: the page merge changed three attributes to refs, and every checkout's kept target/program-store and target/runs/test-store refused to open (seon.db/open!: :seon.db/types-differ, another value type than the schema declares). bin/test failed at its plan, and process tests at root start. Both are regenerable output, made again from their inputs, never records. Fix: seon.db/schema-digest names the schema; seon.test-store/kept-store! answers base-<digest> and removes a store at base of another schema (base itself, or base-<8 hex digits>), sparing a runs directory beside it. The test runner's program store and the process store (seon.test-store/process-store, made by the plan's seon.test-store/make-process-store!, which replaces bin/test's seed step) are named by it. A changed schema makes a new store; nothing is migrated or refused."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.test-store-test/a-kept-store-is-keyed-by-its-schema}}]
